# Advanced Customization 🎨

## Edit Form Customization

```python
@admin.register(Article)
class ArticleAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):
    # Which fields to show in edit form
    fields = ['title', 'slug', 'content', 'category', 'tags', 'status']

    # Or exclude fields
    exclude = ['created_by']

    # Read-only fields
    readonly_fields = ['created', 'updated', 'view_count']

    # Auto-generate slug from title
    prepopulated_fields = {'slug': ('title',)}

    # Organize with fieldsets
    fieldsets = [
        ('Content', {
            'fields': ['title', 'slug', 'content']
        }),
        ('Categorization', {
            'fields': ['category', 'tags']
        }),
        ('Publishing', {
            'fields': ['status', 'published'],
            'classes': ['collapse']  # Collapsible section
        }),
    ]
```

## Inline Models

```python
# Edit related objects on same page
class CommentInline(admin.TabularInline):  # or StackedInline
    model = Comment
    extra = 1  # Number of empty forms

@admin.register(Article)
class ArticleAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):
    inlines = [CommentInline]
```

## Custom Actions

```python
@admin.register(Article)
class ArticleAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):
    actions = ['make_published', 'make_draft']

    @admin.action(description='Mark selected as published')
    def make_published(self, request, queryset):
        queryset.update(status='published')
        self.message_user(request, f'{queryset.count()} articles published.')
```

# Additional Features 🔧

## List Editable

```python
@admin.register(Article)
class ArticleAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):
    list_display = ['title', 'status', 'category', 'is_featured']
    list_editable = ['status', 'is_featured']  # Editable in list view!
```

## Custom Display Functions

```python
@admin.register(Article)
class ArticleAdmin(admin.ModelAdmin):
    list_display = ['title', 'author_name', 'word_count', 'status_badge']

    @admin.display(description='Author')
    def author_name(self, obj):
        return obj.author.get_full_name() or obj.author.username

    @admin.display(description='Words')
    def word_count(self, obj):
        return len(obj.content.split())

    @admin.display(description='Status')
    def status_badge(self, obj):
        colors = {'draft': 'red', 'published': 'green'}
        return format_html(
            '<span style="color: {}">{}</span>',
            colors.get(obj.status, 'gray'),
            obj.status
        )
```

## Admin Site Customization

```python
# admin.py
admin.site.site_header = 'My Blog Admin'
admin.site.site_title = 'Blog Admin Portal'
admin.site.index_title = 'Welcome to the Admin Panel'
```

